<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  One overridden string, and it earns its file.

  The installer closes Windows Explorer and starts it again, and clears Windows' icon cache while
  it is down. Those are the two things about it a user cannot guess and would reasonably be
  alarmed by, and there is nowhere else to say so: the licence page is the licence, and the
  progress bar is too late. WixUI declares its own strings Overridable, so redefining this one
  here replaces it.

  The line breaks are character references rather than actual newlines. An XML parser normalises
  a literal newline inside an attribute value to a space, so writing the paragraphs out over
  several lines produces one run-on paragraph in the dialog.
-->

<WixLocalization Culture="en-us" xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxl">

  <String Id="WelcomeDlgDescription" Value="The Setup Wizard will install [ProductName] on your computer.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Windows Explorer will be closed and restarted during the installation. FlickGit's context menu runs inside Explorer, so this is the only way to replace it — any open Explorer windows will close. Windows' cached icons are cleared at the same time, so icons across the system are redrawn once afterwards.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Click Next to continue or Cancel to exit." />

</WixLocalization>
